{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules","id":823623,"title":"Starting a new game - any suggested house rules or commonly overlooked actual rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-04T12:43:43-08:00","id":823623,"title":"Starting a new game - any suggested house rules or commonly overlooked actual rules?","content":"So I've gone through the 2nd ed core book about twice and I'm having some players over to write up characters this weekend. I'm super excited about the game, but I haven't played any nWoD system games before (I've only run oWoD in the past). Do you guys have any suggestions for starting to GM my first Werewolf game?<br /> <br /> Specifically, I'm looking for house rules you've found helpful, actual rules I might have overlooked, or just suggestions about what to expect from the system (like, how combat flows, etc)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11158-avalon-polo","name":"Avalon Polo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T12:54:43-08:00","id":823638,"title":"","content":"It's easy to overlook the contagiousness of death rage, but the big thing I've seen a lot of people misunderstand has been the choice of personalized suites of triggers. Basically you pick one group, like the Blood, the Other, or Moon triggers on p103, and they apply to your character. This way different members of the pack can have different triggers. Though there are a few triggers at the end of the list applicable to all werewolves.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that Sacred Prey is not 'only prey.' No one is forced to only hunt their sacred prey. Also, with the opening up of rites, only one member of a pack really needs to have the Sacred Hunt rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T13:02:33-08:00","id":823641,"title":"","content":"I would recommend against any sort of proactive house ruling until you have a better feel for the system: the system as printed was designed to work for most groups, most of the time; house rules are designed to work for one group, and one group only.<br /> <br /> I would, however, recommend for establishing &quot;table rules&quot;: expectations for the players. My table rules are:<br /> <br /> 1) Players must create characters that will participate in the story: this is a CofD game, not a mundane life simulator.<br /> 2) Player versus Player social rolls are only allowed if <i>both</i> players agree to the roll <i>and</i> the &quot;defending&quot; character is genuinely on the fence about an action.<br /> 3) Combat PvP is a no.<br /> <br /> Rule 3 applies only to deadly force, if two character want to spar and use dice to determine the winner, that's fine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T13:03:16-08:00","id":823643,"title":"","content":"Gotcha. Yeah, I really like the personalized trigger idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11158-avalon-polo","name":"Avalon Polo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T13:47:33-08:00","id":823675,"title":"","content":"I actually disagree about no PvP, even when it comes to combat. <i>that said</i> I have a regular group that I know enjoys that kind of play and that I trust to handle it maturely. If I was running for a new or unknown group I would not want to allow PvP.<br /> <br /> I like to give everyone an extra Shadow Gift at character creation. Doesn't have a huge impact but it makes for a slightly higher power game out of the gate. I also use the extra Auspices from Signs of the Moon (except for Stellar Eclipse, because I didn't want to convert the Moon Gift and &quot;stellar eclipses&quot; aren't a thing anyway).<br /> <br /> I would recommend running the game by RAW your first time and adjusting with house rules to suit your taste once you've got a good feel for the baseline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T22:20:32-08:00","id":824015,"title":"","content":"I'm sorta with Charlaquin,and I'd even say no to proindrakenzol's second suggestion. To me, only the first one makes perfect sense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T00:22:05-08:00","id":824077,"title":"","content":"This isn't a house rule, but just one piece of advice I find essential to Chronicles of Darkness. Make sure to apply modifiers to dice rolls frequently (when appropriate). As a storyteller you're often too distracted a lot of the time so I make it a habit of every time someone rolls the dice asking myself whether there should be a modifier. The system expects it in a lot of places, there's a lot of abilities that interact with modifiers that never get used if you don't. Most dice rolls should have at least a +1 if there's something making it easier or a -1 if there's something making it more difficult. <br /> <br /> Don't be afraid to use conditions frequently. They're hard to get used to but they're one of the main sources of XP in the new system, use them wherever you can.<br /> <br /> Werewolf gifts can be quite powerful right out of the gate. It's not like the old game where you worked your way through weak abilities to get to strong abilities. They're all amazingly powerful and useful, you just get more dice and a more varied range as you get more powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T00:28:14-08:00","id":824079,"title":"","content":"I thought each character picked a death rage trigger for each of the three levels, and I swear Chris has said it on the forums, too. So you're not affected <i>only</i> by blood, wounds, OR your moon auspice, but could be by all three (but only one type per degree). So when you're high Harmony your moon is a common trigger, but at middle Harmony only wounds bug you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T04:07:38-08:00","id":824159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=824079#post824079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought each character picked a death rage trigger for each of the three levels, and I swear Chris has said it on the forums, too. So you're not affected <i>only</i> by blood, wounds, OR your moon auspice, but could be by all three (but only one type per degree). So when you're high Harmony your moon is a common trigger, but at middle Harmony only wounds bug you</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I was actually wrong on that. However, I can confirm from using it in actual play that it works fine as an alternate to the core system.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T04:25:35-08:00","id":824170,"title":"","content":"Isn't combat PvP generally how wolves settle alpha issues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T04:54:44-08:00","id":824181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=824159#post824159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I was actually wrong on that. However, I can confirm from using it in actual play that it works fine as an alternate to the core system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, huh. Yeah I don't see why it wouldn't work","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T08:19:31-08:00","id":824325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=824181#post824181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, huh. Yeah I don't see why it wouldn't work</div> </div> </div> </div>It works fine if you want to run it that way. I prefer to use all three from the same category because to me it's weird that (for example) at extreme Harmony levels you'd be driven to Kuruth just from your Auspice moon being in the sky, but as you get more balanced suddenly the moon doesn't bother you at all but now the taste of human blood really gets you steamed. And then you get even more balanced and blood doesn't matter any more, but now you just can't stand being targeted by supernatural abilities. I just prefer the consistency of sticking with one type of trigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:55:07-08:00","id":824392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=824170#post824170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't combat PvP generally how wolves settle alpha issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing written about that. If someone challenged my Ithaeur he'd pick a game of Jenga to settle it.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://myfunnymemes.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/The-Most-Intense-Game-Of-Jenga-On-Tumblr.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 02-05-2016, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T06:48:32-08:00","id":824920,"title":"","content":"I have a bit of a problem with Kuruth triggers in a sense that some of them are a lot more broad than the other. &quot;Seeing someone attack a Pack member&quot; is a lot more common than interacting with Wound spirits. Hell, maybe for some narrative reasons you don't want to have Wounds in your chronicle and the trigger never will apply. Similar thing with Blood trigger, it seems that between tasting and swallowing blood you leave choice to the player (unless you design some convoluted scene where villains force-feed human blood to the PC) while other PC can be triggered by Death Rage on some fancy party when a hapless vampire tries to seduce/dominate him with no choice left to him.<br /> <br /> There's no easy and perfect answer how to solve that, but I personally would every lunar month (or other miscellaneous circumstance like maybe meeting a Lune corresponding to the Auspice) roll or make player choose new Kuruth trigger, also among <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers\">new ones made on forum</a>.<br /> <br /> Or maybe just choose 2 and alternate them depending on the Harmony - &quot;The Other&quot; trigger could apply to higher harmony werewolves and &quot;Territory&quot; to lower.<br /> <br /> Also look on the new <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/432182-new-blood-and-bone-archetypes\">Blood &amp; Bone archetypes</a> for more character customization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7871,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","user":"Miriander","date":". 02-06-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T08:24:25-08:00","id":824947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miriander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=824920#post824920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Seeing someone attack a Pack member&quot; is a lot more common than interacting with Wound spirits. Hell, maybe for some narrative reasons you don't want to have Wounds in your chronicle and the trigger never will apply. Similar thing with Blood trigger, it seems that between tasting and swallowing blood you leave choice to the player (unless you design some convoluted scene where villains force-feed human blood to the PC) while other PC can be triggered by Death Rage on some fancy party when a hapless vampire tries to seduce/dominate him with no choice left to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>How common these things are is really going to depend on the Storyteller. If a player picks a trigger based around Wounds and they don't have any Wounds in the game they've sort of dropped the ball. It's worth noting that if you make a bite attack on anything living, or a vampire using blush of life, you're going to be tasting blood. Swallowing blood will pop up a lot if you end up eating people for Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T09:47:28-08:00","id":824971,"title":"","content":"If I figure a player of mine picked a trigger merely for it's unlikeliness, you can bet the next session will involve it, one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T10:16:23-08:00","id":824981,"title":"","content":"I agree with Ephsy, although I come at it from a slightly different angle. To me, a player choosing Wounds as their trigger is a signal that that player wants to explore Wounds and interact with Wound-Born spirits in the game. A player choosing Blood as their Trigger is signaling that they want cannibalism (whether intentional or forced) to feature in the game. A player choosing Moon as their Trigger is telling me they want me to keep track of the lunar phases in the game and give them a very horror movie &quot;fear the moon&quot; kind of experience.<br /> <br /> Playing into the PCs' Kuruth Triggers is not a punishment, it's a way to deliver on the kind of horror and drama that they are interested in. If the player <i>percieves</i> it as a punishment, it's time to sit down and have a talk about expectations and table etiquette. If a player wants to play up a particular kind of horror that you're not really interested in focusing on in this story, it's OK to just tell them &quot;I don't think that Trigger is likely to come up in this story. You should pick a different one.&quot; It's also OK to discuss the possibility of a compromise. Maybe you didn't originally plan on involving wounds, but the player <i>really</i> wants them, so you work in a subplot to explore that idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-06-2016, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T14:24:40-08:00","id":825096,"title":"","content":"Agreed.<br /> <br /> For example, my character picked up Hunger as his trigger. At Primal Urge 1 or 2, it won't be a problem, but as he gains experience in the Great Hunt, his appetites become more and more demanding. He doesn't needs to subsist exclusively on spiritual essence, but he choose to do so already. It plays rather well considering that he's a Meninna Ithaeur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T14:31:23-08:00","id":825101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=825096#post825096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed.<br /> <br /> For example, my character picked up Hunger as his trigger. At Primal Urge 1 or 2, it won't be a problem, but as he gains experience in the Great Hunt, his appetites become more and more demanding. He doesn't needs to subsist exclusively on spiritual essence, but he choose to do so already. It plays rather well considering that he's a Meninna Ithaeur.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really cool custom Trigger!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T21:59:25-08:00","id":825263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=824170#post824170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't combat PvP generally how wolves settle alpha issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd consider that &quot;sparring&quot; since the goal isn't to kill the other player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T22:18:29-08:00","id":825275,"title":"","content":"Some less Werewolf-specific points:<ul><li>Conditions are fluid. Don't keep flipping back and forth through the book to reference their strict rules every time one comes into play. Keep play flowing. Make new Conditions; resolve existing ones when it makes sense that they've been resolved; make up mechanical effects on the fly for new or existing Conditions as seems appropriate. Conditions caused by player abilities, like the Hunter's Aspect or Conditions specifically written to be caused by a given Gift Facet, are a partial exception. The player invests in being able to cause those and can plan around using them, so they should find their effects relatively reliable.</li> <li>Willpower is fluid. Let your players know they should burn it whenever they're counting on something to go through, and don't be strict about letting them recover it with their Blood and Bone. Easy come, easy go.</li> <li>Proper combat is for maiming or killing things. That's definitely going to come up, but for lower-key scenarios (sparring or a non-lethal battle challenge seem relevant), use the Down &amp; Dirty rules. They're faster, too.</li> <li>Something people with oWoD experience sometimes stumble with when trying out nWoD: nWoD doesn't have the kind of success gradient oWoD did. oWoD had rolls where your number of successes mattered, but in nWoD, outside of combat rolls, contested actions and extended actions, the default state is there are only three quantities that matter: zero (you fail), between zero and five (you succeed), and five or more (exceptional success). Successful dice aren't as common but you don't need as many of them.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T17:31:45-08:00","id":825671,"title":"","content":"I would recommend getting rid of beats for resolving conditions. It causes all kinds of strange metagaming and weirdness. Give beats for exceptional roleplaying / tactics to compensate. The beats you get from persistent conditions are fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 02-07-2016, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T23:15:26-08:00","id":825796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=825671#post825671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would recommend getting rid of beats for resolving conditions. It causes all kinds of strange metagaming and weirdness. Give beats for exceptional roleplaying / tactics to compensate. The beats you get from persistent conditions are fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am completely on the other side of the fence. For once playing into what was done to a character is beneficial to the player. (like if he was swayed by someone pretty, or got angry at a packmate)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T00:42:24-08:00","id":825824,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I incline with Griautis. At least give those rules a spin before you decide whether they're working for your group or not. My group hasn't had any problems with Condition beats warping the game, and they key into the Condition rules in such a way that if you get rid of them you should at least replace them with something (Willpower points work).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T05:33:51-08:00","id":825933,"title":"","content":"In the end, if you feel like going for a Conditions beat would make no sense for the character.. then why does he have that condition? And how could he resolve that condition for it to make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T06:00:33-08:00","id":825947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=825824#post825824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least give those rules a spin before you decide whether they're working for your group or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, definitely. Give both versions a spin and see which of the two works best at your table. The downside to asking for House Rules up front is never getting to see for yourself why some things don't work / are broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T11:54:40-08:00","id":826119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=825947#post825947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, definitely. Give both versions a spin and see which of the two works best at your table. The downside to asking for House Rules up front is never getting to see for yourself why some things don't work / are broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>They might not work for your game but they are by no means broken. They work incredibly for my group, and many people who post here attest the same. <i>That's</i> the downside of asking for house rules, you never get to see if the rule you're &quot;fixing&quot; was actually broken, or if the person who suggested that house rule just had a play style that didn't mesh well with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:49:14-08:00","id":826386,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What do people think about being able to harvest essence from slain spirits without having to use the Siskur-Dah rite?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's a house rule Mr. Shopping did in Detroit Rock City, but that was a pretty atypical game in that they were forced off their territory and then into a brutal death grind. I don't think they would have survived if they couldn't get essence off of the spirits that they fought, so maybe it is one of those situations where the rule is right for that game and not necessarily for every game.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T20:34:46-08:00","id":826507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826119#post826119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might not work for your game but they are by no means broken. They work incredibly for my group, and many people who post here attest the same. <i>That's</i> the downside of asking for house rules, you never get to see if the rule you're &quot;fixing&quot; was actually broken, or if the person who suggested that house rule just had a play style that didn't mesh well with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with awarding beats for resolving conditions is...<ul><li>Some players will intentionally try to resolve them quickly to gain a beat, instead of doing what makes the most sense for their character.</li> <li>Some players will intentionally NOT resolve them quickly, to avoid looking like the kind of player who is constantly trying to get beats.</li> <li>Some players might not want to resolve some of them, but feel like they must to keep up with the amount of beats other players have.</li> <li>Some players might want to resolve them, but feel bad about getting so many more beats than their friends.</li> <li>Some players do none of the above, but still feel stressed out and worry that they will be tempted one way or another.</li> <li>Some players are just lucky.</li> <li>Some storytellers hand conditions out normally, then discover their players are advancing too quickly.</li> <li>Some storytellers are afraid to hand out conditions, because they do not want their players advancing so quickly.<br /> (This is not suggesting that the advancement pace is too fast, just that some storytellers feel like it is)</li> <li>Some storytellers feel pressured to hand out more conditions to increase how fast their players are advancing.<br /> (They could just award more beats. No idea why they feel this way.)</li> <li>Some storytellers feel like some players are advancing much faster than others.</li> <li>Some builds can generate conditions and resolve them at mind blowing speeds.</li> <li>Even some simple combos (no more than 1-2 parts) generate and resolve conditions pretty fast.</li> <li>Inspired is a lean mean beat generating machine.</li> <li>Extended Actions are lean mean beat generating machines.</li> <li>Extra bookwork just keeping track of who resolved what and when.</li> </ul>Some of those overlap, but those were just the ones that come immediately to mind. Every single one of those can be fixed in various ways: <i>Use Group Beats. Nerf Inspired. Don't Play With (Negative Attribute) Players. Stop Sucking.</i> And these are all genuinely good solutions to some of the previously listed problems! But removing beats for resolving conditions? That has almost no negative consequences at all, as long as you are providing some additional beats from other sources. (I enjoy giving beats for good roleplaying / good ideas, but your preference may vary)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T20:42:32-08:00","id":826511,"title":"","content":"The problem with &quot;Some players...&quot; Prepositions?<br /> <br /> Some players may take a dump on your floor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T21:05:17-08:00","id":826521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826511#post826511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with &quot;Some players...&quot; Prepositions?<br /> Some players may take a dump on your floor.</div> </div> </div> </div>A literary eccentricity to add personal enjoyment when writing the post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T21:18:51-08:00","id":826532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But removing beats for resolving conditions? That has almost no negative consequences at all, as long as you are providing some additional beats from other sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some players don't role-play things their characters should be feeling.<br /> <br /> Conditions gives incentive to do so. Removing them takes them back to playing the character sheet, not the character.<br /> <br /> And the biggie. Conditions give players the power to determine how they get Beats and Experience. Removing that places it solely in the hands of the Storyteller, who may deem that they're 'advancing too quickly' and stop rewarding them for the kinds of things that had given them rewards in previous sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-09-2016, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T21:42:18-08:00","id":826550,"title":"","content":"Homosexual sex still creates a Unihar ghost baby that chases the parents to their doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T21:53:59-08:00","id":826557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826532#post826532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some players don't role-play things their characters should be feeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an issue to be discussed between games, establish expectations, etc, etc. Not something to be done with pavlov beats (all of this is in my humble opinion, of course).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826532#post826532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conditions gives incentive to do so. Removing them takes them back to playing the character sheet, not the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>My anecdotal experience is the opposite. Keeping them takes the player out of the character.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826532#post826532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the biggie. Conditions give players the power to determine how they get Beats and Experience. Removing that places it solely in the hands of the Storyteller, who may deem that they're 'advancing too quickly' and stop rewarding them for the kinds of things that had given them rewards in previous sessions.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Fulfill Aspiration --</b> Long Term Aspirations are pretty solidly in the hands of your storyteller, but Short Term Aspirations give players the power to determine how they get Beats and Experience.<br /> <b>Resolve Condition --</b> In dispute here.<br /> <b>Persistent Condition --</b> I am perfectly cool with this one. Gives the players the power to determine how they get Beats and Experience.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure --</b> Literally a choice the player makes. Gives the players the power to determine how they get Beats and Experience.<br /> <b>Lethal Damage --</b> 50/50 here. Players can always turn social encounters into fights and risk getting this. Or go looking for fights. Kind of playing with fire. Werewolves have an easier time of it though.<br /> <b>End of Session --</b> Automatic.<br /> <br /> You are free to disagree with me here, but I do not see any shortage of players being able to determine how they get Beats and Experience. Removing beats from resolving conditions does reduce the frequency this happens by the technical definition of reduce, but there is no great deficit created. I mentioned previously that I was in favor of rewarding beats for good roleplaying / good ideas. I actually believe that rewarding good roleplaying / good ideas is a far more effective way to get a player to focus upon her character instead of the sheet (did you know they actually removed the ability to gain beats for roleplaying?) But if your players are concerned about favoritism, then I might encourage you to double the beats gained from some of the other methods listed here (except End of Session). This is especially neat with aspirations and dramatic failures! I'm always open to more options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":".  Grammar. 02-09-2016, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T22:43:40-08:00","id":826576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some players will intentionally try to resolve them quickly to gain a beat, instead of doing what makes the most sense for their character.</div> </div> </div> </div>But resolving beats requires the character to behave in a way that is consistent with what the Condition represents, so I don't see how this is a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some players will intentionally NOT resolve them quickly, to avoid looking like the kind of player who is constantly trying to get beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is only a problem if you shame your players for trying to get Beats. Don't do that. If your players shame each other for it, tell them to stop being immature and knock it off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some players might not want to resolve some of them, but feel like they must to keep up with the amount of beats other players have.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is a problem for your group, that's what the optional Group Beats rule exists for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some players might want to resolve them, but feel bad about getting so many more beats than their friends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, if this is a problem for your group, use Group Beats<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some players do none of the above, but still feel stressed out and worry that they will be tempted one way or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>This can generally be avoided by having a positive group dynamic. Again, don't shame your players for doing things that make sense from a meta-game standpoint, and this won't be an issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some players are just lucky.</div> </div> </div> </div>They sure are. What's this got to do with Beats again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some storytellers hand conditions out normally, then discover their players are advancing too quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>...So adjust the rate you hand them out at?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some storytellers are afraid to hand out conditions, because they do not want their players advancing so quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly is wrong with players advancing again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(This is not suggesting that the advancement pace is too fast, just that some storytellers feel like it is)</div> </div> </div> </div>K.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some storytellers feel pressured to hand out more conditions to increase how fast their players are advancing.</div> </div> </div> </div>...So do that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(They could just award more beats. No idea why they feel this way.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Who exactly are they and can you name four of them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some storytellers feel like some players are advancing much faster than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Group Beats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some builds can generate conditions and resolve them at mind blowing speeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure this falls into &quot;feature, not bug&quot; territory, but if you disagree you should consider using the Group Beats rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even some simple combos (no more than 1-2 parts) generate and resolve conditions pretty fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhuh. Group Beats if you find that to be a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inspired is a lean mean beat generating machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sensing a pattern here...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extended Actions are lean mean beat generating machines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Say it with me, now: &quot;If this is a problem for your group, consider using the optional Group Beats rule.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extra bookwork just keeping track of who resolved what and when.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a drawback of the Beat system, yes. Condition cards can be very helpful with this, but it's definitely a trade-off. YMMV on if it's worth the added bookkeeping. That's one of the reasons you should try it out and see how it works for you before just dismissing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826507#post826507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of those overlap, but those were just the ones that come immediately to mind. Every single one of those can be fixed in various ways: <i>Use Group Beats. Nerf Inspired. Don't Play With (Negative Attribute) Players. Stop Sucking.</i> And these are all genuinely good solutions to some of the previously listed problems! But removing beats for resolving conditions? That has almost no negative consequences at all, as long as you are providing some additional beats from other sources. (I enjoy giving beats for good roleplaying / good ideas, but your preference may vary)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's entirely subjective if any of these are actually problems, and if they are, almost every single one of them can be resolved by using Group Beats. Those that can't can pretty much be resolved by the &quot;don't be a jerk&quot; rule. The drawback of getting rid of Beats for resolving Conditions is that you lose a very powerful incentive to actually play into your Conditions. Some Conditions like Shaken and Spooked become literally useless because they were designed under the assumption that players will be willing to Resolve them for the Beat. Again, it's a tradeoff, and for some people (such as yourself, evidently) it's not worth it. For other people it is. That's why, as per my original point, you should try things out as written before houseruling them, so you can see if it actually causes problems for your group, or if you have a different experience than the person who wrote the houserule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-09-2016, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T22:47:08-08:00","id":826579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiwass</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826550#post826550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homosexual sex still creates a Unihar ghost baby that chases the parents to their doom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... As of 2e, no sex creates Unihar, heterosexual or otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:37:48-08:00","id":826602,"title":"","content":"(Forgive me for compressing this. There was a lot of repeat material)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826576#post826576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But resolving beats requires the character to behave in a way that is consistent with what the Condition represents, so I don't see how this is a problem. The drawback of getting rid of Beats for resolving Conditions is that you lose a very powerful incentive to actually play into your Conditions.[/</div> </div> </div> </div>In some cases you are right. In some cases you are wrong. Swaggering certainly does not. Mystified certainly does not. Confused certainly does not. Berserk certainly does not. And so on, and so forth. That's on top of being taken out of your character to browse your condition flashcards / flip through your book / check your laptop to remind yourself what they do and how to resolve them. There are lots.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826576#post826576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is only a problem if you shame your players for trying to get Beats. Don't do that. If your players shame each other for it, tell them to stop being immature and knock it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Decades of socialization against 'powergamers' makes people shame themselves plenty for having those thoughts. You're not getting rid of that anytime soon.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826576#post826576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this is a problem for your group, that's what the optional Group Beats rule exists for.<br /> Group Beats.<br /> Group Beats rule.<br /> Uhuh. Group Beats<br /> I'm sensing a pattern here...<br /> Group Beats rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely did! I wish I could convince a bunch of other groups to use it. I weep a little inside every time I see a gaming group with players who want to use it but a storyteller who does not because it is 'optional'. Heck, not even <i><b>on</b></i>e person in this thread recommended it to the OP before we got on the topic.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826576#post826576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They sure are. What's this got to do with Beats again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exceptional Successes = Conditions = Beats.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826576#post826576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who exactly are they and can you name four of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused by what you mean, here.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826576#post826576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is wrong with players advancing again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some storytellers are uncomfortable with it. They feel like they cannot make meaningful challenges, or as players become increasingly specialized they worry that creating a challenge for one character will devastate another character. The usual slew of problems people run into before they ascend to Storyteller Perfection.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826576#post826576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...So do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally prefer to hand out conditions based on what the characters actually do / what happens to them. Not just to advance characters arbitrarily.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826576#post826576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one of the reasons you should try it out and see how it works for you before just dismissing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I definitely recommend the OP give both versions a try!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 02-09-2016, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:56:05-08:00","id":826613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiwass</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826550#post826550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homosexual sex still creates a Unihar ghost baby that chases the parents to their doom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even close. Are you deliberately trolling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T02:57:16-08:00","id":826670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826602#post826602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, not even <i><b>on</b></i>e person in this thread recommended it to the OP before we got on the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is more charitable to assume that it wasn't mentioned because optional rules in the books aren't exactly things people consider house rules to bring up in a thread asking for suggestions on such.<br /> <br /> Also, if a group is seriously having problems with Condition-to-Beat rates, consider using the GMCRU Beats guideline instead of the ones the 2e core books have used were you can only get one Resolution Beat per scene. There's no incentive to horde them in significant quantity, there's more incentive to spend them since letting them pile up doesn't do you any good, there's far less pressure on expectations (both on players and STs) when everyone's getting one Resolution per scene, and &quot;beat machine&quot; builds aren't really a big deal and/or are most effective if used for the whole group (exceptional successes can be used to give the other PCs Conditions so they have something to resolve because again hording them for yourself doesn't do you much).<br /> <br /> Heck, it pretty much eliminates your whole list of problems because it breaks down to, &quot;expect 1 Beat per scene from resolving Conditions.&quot; so player and ST expectations are easily aligned; esp. with a simply &quot;don't be a dick&quot; move. It even gets around any pesky &quot;years of indoctrination&quot; against certain playstyles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm confused by what you mean, here. </div> </div> </div>Appealing to vague people that we can only take exist and have the point of view you claim they do on your say-so is a fundamentally worthless statement. All it comes down to is, &quot;You should value my post more because I made up people that agree with me to make my point look stronger.&quot; It doesn't matter if they're real people or not. For the purpose you're putting them towards in your post, they only exist as an artificial way to make your points look stronger than they might on their face. Of course this is a general conversation, not a formal debate, and esp. online with respect to other people's privacy, giving details on people to cite as supporters of your position isn't really viable; but that only adds to why the tactic isn't worth using in esoteric discussions. What does it matter if four people you know agree with you, but forty people I know agree with me?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T03:27:47-08:00","id":826682,"title":"","content":"You can always put a Beats Per Session limit, and be done with the infinite loop things and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T04:49:35-08:00","id":826701,"title":"","content":"I think Aiwass was suggesting that as a houserule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:34:58-08:00","id":826887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826670#post826670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, it pretty much eliminates your whole list of problems because it breaks down to, &quot;expect 1 Beat per scene from resolving Conditions.&quot; so player and ST expectations are easily aligned; esp. with a simply &quot;don't be a dick&quot; move. It even gets around any pesky &quot;years of indoctrination&quot; against certain playstyles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I definitely agree that it does solve most of the problems. We can add that to the list of things for the OP to try out, and see how well it works for him. To clarify for the OP, the rule fear resolving conditions used to be:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Some rolls and powers may impart Conditions on your character. Each Condition has criteria for resolution, usually requiring a difficult choice for the character. If resolved, take a Beat. You may only take one Beat for a Condition in a given scene.&quot;</span></span></i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826670#post826670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Appealing to vague people that we can only take exist and have the point of view you claim they do on your say-so is a fundamentally worthless statement. All it comes down to is, &quot;You should value my post more because I made up people that agree with me to make my point look stronger.&quot; It doesn't matter if they're real people or not. For the purpose you're putting them towards in your post, they only exist as an artificial way to make your points look stronger than they might on their face. Of course this is a general conversation, not a formal debate, and esp. online with respect to other people's privacy, giving details on people to cite as supporters of your position isn't really viable; but that only adds to why the tactic isn't worth using in esoteric discussions. What does it matter if four people you know agree with you, but forty people I know agree with me?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I was confused about what she meant. Asking people for names on the internet is like asking for their educational history. Nobody is going to believe it even if you are telling the truth. Heck, it would accomplish nothing AND probably make one of the named friends come after me with a (mostly harmless) revenge prank. That's an Admiral Ackbar level trap!<br /> <br /> So I'm not sure why she asked for names. I could have misunderstood something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:35:32-08:00","id":826889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826670#post826670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Appealing to vague people that we can only take exist and have the point of view you claim they do on your say-so is a fundamentally worthless statement. All it comes down to is, &quot;You should value my post more because I made up people that agree with me to make my point look stronger.&quot; It doesn't matter if they're real people or not. For the purpose you're putting them towards in your post, they only exist as an artificial way to make your points look stronger than they might on their face. Of course this is a general conversation, not a formal debate, and esp. online with respect to other people's privacy, giving details on people to cite as supporters of your position isn't really viable; but that only adds to why the tactic isn't worth using in esoteric discussions. What does it matter if four people you know agree with you, but forty people I know agree with me?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hence my previous post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:02:12-08:00","id":826902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826602#post826602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Forgive me for compressing this. There was a lot of repeat material)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, good call there. I probably should have done the same in my post. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826602#post826602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In some cases you are right. In some cases you are wrong. Swaggering certainly does not. Mystified certainly does not. Confused certainly does not. Berserk certainly does not. And so on, and so forth. That's on top of being taken out of your character to browse your condition flashcards / flip through your book / check your laptop to remind yourself what they do and how to resolve them. There are lots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I phrased that poorly. Some Conditions are resolved by doing things a person in that state would do, and some are resolved by facing complications that could conceivably be caused by doing things a person in that state would do. The point is, they're supposed to reward you for doing things that heighten the drama. If players are wailing on each other to fill up their health tracks with damage and resolve the Swaggering Condition instead of going out to fight werewolves like the Condition says, they're breaking the &quot;don't be a jerk&quot; rule. In my opinion, the most important rule in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826602#post826602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Decades of socialization against 'powergamers' makes people shame themselves plenty for having those thoughts. You're not getting rid of that anytime soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>So shouldn't we be working towards breaking down that stigma instead of complacently letting it continue unchallenged? Maybe try telling your players that it's ok to do things that make sense from a character optimization standpoint (provided they continue to respect the &quot;don't be a jerk&quot; rule) instead of house ruling to deny them opporties to make those choices. You might be surprised by the results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826602#post826602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely did! I wish I could convince a bunch of other groups to use it. I weep a little inside every time I see a gaming group with players who want to use it but a storyteller who does not because it is 'optional'. Heck, not even <i><b>on</b></i>e person in this thread recommended it to the OP before we got on the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, it's not a house rule, so it probably didn't occur to most people to suggest it in this thread asking about house rules. But yeah, Group Beats is a great rule. I don't personally use it, because my players prefer their characters to advance individually and are okay with the fact that it will sometimes mean they fall behind other characters. It's something we have talked about many times as a group, and constantly re-assess in case someone decides it's not working for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826602#post826602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exceptional Successes = Conditions = Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, this is my fault. I understood what you meant, I was just being glib and trying to hint that I don't see it as an issue. Ultimately, it's another factor that can lead to asymmetrical character advancement, which may or may not be a problem for a given group. If it is a problem, Group Beats is a great solution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826602#post826602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused by what you mean, here.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant was, you're talking a lot about &quot;some players&quot; and &quot;some STs&quot;, but I don't know who &quot;they&quot; are. Which isn't to say I don't think there are players or STs who experience these issues. But I don't think it's worthwhile to make house rules based on what &quot;some people&quot; experience. If it's a problem for you and your group, or you know someone for whom it has been a problem, that's a different story. I wasn't literally asking for your friends' names or anything, I was just trying to illustrate that there's not much meaning in the experiences of vague, unknown, &quot;them&quot;, and that shouldn't be a deciding factor in whether or not to house rule something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826602#post826602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some storytellers are uncomfortable with it. They feel like they cannot make meaningful challenges, or as players become increasingly specialized they worry that creating a challenge for one character will devastate another character. The usual slew of problems people run into before they ascend to Storyteller Perfection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. That's something that takes experience to find what works for you. The thing is, I don't think RPG rules should be designed based on trying to avoid anything a new GM might struggle with. They should provide experienced GMs with tools to run great games, and provide new GMs with advice on how to make the most out of those tools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826602#post826602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally prefer to hand out conditions based on what the characters actually do / what happens to them. Not just to advance characters arbitrarily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, so do that. I fail to see how this particular line of discussion points to a flaw in the Beats and Conditions system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826602#post826602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I definitely recommend the OP give both versions a try!</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-09-2016, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:14:04-08:00","id":826989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826902#post826902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is, they're supposed to reward you for doing things that heighten the drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is better to directly reward people for doing things that heighten the drama.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826902#post826902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So shouldn't we be working towards breaking down that stigma instead of complacently letting it continue unchallenged? Maybe try telling your players that it's ok to do things that make sense from a character optimization standpoint (provided they continue to respect the &quot;don't be a jerk&quot; rule) instead of house ruling to deny them opporties to make those choices<br /> <br /> Sure. That's something that takes experience to find what works for you. The thing is, I don't think RPG rules should be designed based on trying to avoid anything a new GM might struggle with. They should provide experienced GMs with tools to run great games, and provide new GMs with advice on how to make the most out of those tools.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree on a pretty fundamental level here. I don't think these are the kinds of situations where you choose only a single path. I think we should do both! Have idealized goals that everyone strides towards, AND build bridges that help make the journey easier.<br /> <br /> Also, I know that this is all for the benefit of the OP, but we may be getting to the 'Agree To Disagree' stage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T05:18:47-08:00","id":827427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826613#post826613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not even close. Are you deliberately trolling?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not even. I'm deliberately talking about house rules. Super seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T05:22:14-08:00","id":827430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=826579#post826579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err... As of 2e, no sex creates Unihar, heterosexual or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read 2e wolfman yet. I will, but probably won't run it. But still, very legit house rule to bring back unihars to punish randy furries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T09:03:54-08:00","id":827548,"title":"","content":"Why is there any need to punish &quot;randy furries?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Unihar didn't exist because of that. They existed because it was a concept from WtA that werewolf/werewolf sex should be supernaturally bad. 2e cut them because there's no need for that in Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T09:17:25-08:00","id":827558,"title":"","content":"I've seen a fear expressed among gamers that if you allow romance or sex within games, people will just throw everything off the table and ravage each other carnally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T17:44:47-08:00","id":827885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiwass</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=827427#post827427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even. I'm deliberately talking about house rules. Super seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Piece of advice: You may want to express those kind of ideas better than with a curt sentence, if you want to be treated &quot;super seriously&quot; then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T18:54:58-08:00","id":827916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823623-starting-a-new-game-any-suggested-house-rules-or-commonly-overlooked-actual-rules?p=827885#post827885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Piece of advice: You may want to express those kind of ideas better than with a curt sentence, if you want to be treated &quot;super seriously&quot; then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephsy, I wasn't trolling, but I was being cheeky! It's a cultural thing for me. No offence intended.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T20:54:02-08:00","id":827965,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bYou may think it's being cheeky, the mod staff call it trolling. Stay out of this thread now, ignoring the directive will result in a suspension.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T08:38:30-08:00","id":833305,"title":"","content":"The advice to wait till you've felt out the system, gotten a taste of what the developers intended, before devising house rules is sound.<br /> <br /> However, there is one little tweak that I would totally offer even players just starting out in WtF 2E. You know how Uratha get bans as they drop in Harmony? The lower they get, the more their spirit psychology asserts itself, resulting in bans. I like to add a thematically-appropriate reflection of this on the High Harmony side. At my table, as Harmony rises, they take the Open condition to certain kinds of spirits. The Uratha takes the condition as if they were a location; allowing spirits to manifest in their presence. When they break to Harmony 6, they take something very specific and thematically-appropriate [ie Open(Lust), Open(Revenge), Open(Cahalunim)]. At Harmony 8 the category becomes more general, so that different kinds of spirits can manifest around the Uratha. Finally at Harmony 10, the condition is simply Open, with no specific category. Any ephemeral entity may use the Uratha as a conduit.<br /> <br /> The metaphysical fluff I came up for this is that the Uratha's spiritual side withers and their physical presence roots, allowing spirits to exploit that void and flow across it.<br /> <br /> I've found this small tweak to be mechanically harmonious (no pun intended) with the effects on the reverse end of the Harmony scale. Low Harmony is personal and High Harmony is environmental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2320-tilting-clock","name":"Tilting Clock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T10:40:25-08:00","id":833379,"title":"","content":"That doesn't really meshes with the spiritual division that very high harmony entails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:42:57-08:00","id":833493,"title":"","content":"The difficulty in Reaching reinforces that aspect of Harmony. My houserule is there to inject chaos similar to how bans inject chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2320-tilting-clock","name":"Tilting Clock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:15:44-08:00","id":833622,"title":"","content":"Not to, err, <i>beat</i> a dead horse, but in my CofD game (currently on indefinite hiatus), I award beats based on <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RuleOfDrama\" target=\"_blank\">Rule of Drama</a>/<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RuleOfCool\" target=\"_blank\">Rule of Cool</a>/<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RuleOfFunny\" target=\"_blank\">Rule of Funny</a>. If the players have their characters do something exceptionally dramatic, cool, or funny (and it makes sense), I'll award a beat for it. I'll hand out a beat for exceptional roleplaying. I'll hand out beats if the player characters make headway in the plot, or just come up with a really interesting idea. I basically just reward them for being engaged in the game. This was partly because we started in 1E and were transitioning into 2E, so were still getting used to the Condition rules (and forgot about them entirely more often than not.) After three or four sessions with minimal beats being awarded, I decided to just start handing them out when I felt the players deserved them. Give the Condition rules a try (seriously, they're really good, if a pain to remember/look up a lot of the time), but don't be afraid to hand out beats &quot;just 'cause.&quot; If the characters are advancing quickly, you can always bump up the stats of the bad guys they face to compensate. Or start requiring increasingly exceptional dramatic/cool/funny RP to keep the beats flowing, asking the players to step up their game in that arena.<br /> <br /> And my group used the group beats rule, partly so that everyone would advance at the same rate, and partly because, it being a crossover game, there would be sessions that focused more heavily on one player (the Mage dealing with Magey things, the Promethan dealing with Prometheany things, the Geist dealing with Geisty things, and everyone dealing with Vampirey things), so not everyone would necessarily have the same opportunities to shine in every session. I highly recommend Group Beats, because then the very act of gaining beats brings the table closer together. One great RPer earning beats left and right by being awesome in-character nets everyone beats, one &quot;tanky&quot; combat character taking all the damage (and bad Conditions) is not just keeping the &quot;squishier&quot; characters alive, he's generating beats for them. A lucky player's luck is benefitting the whole group, instead of just them. And so on. It highlights the &quot;co-operative&quot; aspect of &quot;co-operative storytelling.&quot;<br /> <br /> The best piece of advice I would give, starting any game but especially a CofD game, is to talk to the players about what kind of game they want to play and what kind of game you want to run. If you plan to give them a wide-open sandbox where the only thing that moves the story forward is their motivations, and their motivation is to be pointed at an enemy they can slaughter, you're gonna have a bad time. If they want to play in a wide-open sandbox where their motivations are the only thing moving the story forward, and you want to run an episodic monster-of-the-week game, you're gonna have a bad time. CofD has so many tool and types of stories available that it can be rough getting everyone invested in the same kind of story. Being on the same page about what kind of game this will be before a dot is ever put on a character sheet is crucial. You don't want to get five sessions in and have the one player who's been twiddling their thumbs the whole time look up and ask &quot;So when do meet the bad guy so I can kill him?&quot; Or have the player who seems to have been merrily slaughtering everything alongside everyone else take you aside and ask &quot;So when do I get to explore the tortured nature of my monstrous self?&quot; From the very first page of this thread, the piece of advice about requiring the players to make characters who will engage with the troupe and the plot, is an excellent piece of advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}